{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-properties-diagonal-representable}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6e17343295db9ec56a3caf82b82bae2f58de2da5b6b76ce9d19565e074d5ff81", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0e5c504f8d8856160ce006887972d82068a6536dc38b44fa9bcecf61a8371081", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks\nwhich is representable by algebraic spaces. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is representable\n(by schemes),\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is a monomorphism,\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0005> is separated, and\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0006> is locally quasi-finite.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e37042e7b51fcaf9bacac5df134bfd9d638908735c02940ede08dd1937f11e8d", "unit_id": "tag:04YQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$T \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}} \\mathcal{X} \\to T$", "MATH_0004": "$T \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}} \\mathcal{X} \\to T$", "MATH_0005": "$T \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}} \\mathcal{X} \\to T$", "MATH_0006": "$T \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}} \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-properties-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-properties-diagonal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{equation-diagonal}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-criterion-map-representable-spaces-fibred-in-groupoids}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-monomorphism-loc-finite-type-loc-quasi-finite}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-proposition-locally-quasi-finite-separated-over-scheme}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7ffcbd4d38d6465e1cceddf4e30c895581beccced26674f895dea544f58d256e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54b91f5384b0b9fa57a35877ca1576d18698641546e6f3675955ced6be45fe59", "source_text": "We have already seen in\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthat <MATH_0001> is representable by algebraic\nspaces. Hence the statements (2) -- (5) make sense, see\nProperties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0002>.\nAlso\nLemma <REF_0003>\nguarantees (2) holds.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism\nand contemplate Diagram (<REF_0004>). By\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0005>\nthe right vertical arrow is injective as a map of sheaves, i.e., a\nmonomorphism of algebraic spaces. Hence also the morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nis a monomorphism. Thus (3) holds. We already know that\n<MATH_0004>\nis locally of finite type. Thus\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0006>\nallows us to conclude that\n<MATH_0005>\nis locally quasi-finite and separated. This proves (4) and (5).\nFinally,\nMorphisms of Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0007>\nimplies that\n<MATH_0006>\nis a scheme which proves (1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:23900c2b2badc04eba00b8980ec558303bf184572cde2a80a640ddaf425f29cc", "unit_id": "tag:04YQ:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta_f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-separated-diagonal-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b1cb21e35bd6da8a521081e5c7f4df8df36f66e296776ce77acb1476e5c0ba21", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5cda615dc4c7d9bffc2b1089cdc05497ff010c42eb25d158abcecd067b9b379", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces. Then the following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is separated,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is a closed immersion,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is proper, or\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0005> is universally closed.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5bd90a6d01a002f9f66dc53e18e5fe3a86e67cc0554bc69248d06f09e9b2170e", "unit_id": "tag:04YS:statement"}
